m/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98328#pullrequestreview-2631680496","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98328","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98328#pullrequestreview-2631680496"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98328"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-21T02:31:50Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2637982809,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6dPGxZ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally (rebased on top of `master` https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/39c201ca58a8ddf1e99e62c8453294a2662a2fd8), it works as expected.\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- I think this behavior should also apply when running the main scene if its root node is a Node3D. Otherwise, the behavior you get between running the main scene and the current scene differs, which can be unexpected when you're currently editing the main scene.\r\n- The 3 warnings on startup take a lot of space in the editor **Debugger > Errors** panel:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45ad3055-d290-452f-981b-da20835985ed)\r\n\r\nTo resolve this, we should consolidate them into a single warning message that lists the nodes that were added:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCurrent scene was run without WorldEnvironment, DirectionalLight3D and Camera3D nodes. Adding 3 preview nodes to the scene. This will not carry over to the exported project.\r\nYou can disable this by changing `editor/run/automatically_add_preview_nodes_when_running_single_3d_scene` in the Project Settings.\r\n```\r\n\r\n- The setting name is pretty long (I believe it's the longest setting name we have right now). I suggest shortening it to **Add Preview Nodes When Running Scene**. This also makes the setting name agnostic between 2D and 3D, in case we decide to add a preview node system to 2D in the future.\r\n\r\n- There's a visible gray screen flash when the missing nodes are being added (watch the video at 0.5× speed). This does not occur if the nodes were added to the scene before running it. Is there a way we could avoid it, e.g. by disabling the render loop until all preview nodes have been added?\r\n\r\n[video](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17c02fc6-813f-42d0-872b-6956e1c425ea)\r\n\r\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98328#pullrequestreview-2637982809","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98328","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98328#pullrequestreview-2637982809"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98328"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-24T17:58:22Z","commit_id":null}]